// LB+datas -- load buffering through data dependencies, the out-of-thin-air
// shape.
//
// Each thread copies what it read into the other thread's location. Reading
// 42 in both threads justifies itself: each read takes its value from the
// other thread's write, which writes what the other read read.
//
// Source: Batty, Memarian, Nienhuis, Pichon-Pharabod & Sewell, "The Problem of
//   Programming Language Concurrency Semantics" (ESOP 2015) -- the C/C++11
//   axiomatic model has no thin-air axiom and admits this execution at any
//   value; RC11 (Lahav et al., PLDI 2017) forbids it with acyclic(sb | rf).
//
// herd7 is no oracle for this test: it answers Never under cpp11.cat and
// cpp17.cat as under rc11.cat, because its candidate generation computes values
// from read-from edges and never makes one out of a circular dependency.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  r1 := x.load(rlx);
  y.store(r1, rlx)
} ||| {
  r2 := y.load(rlx);
  x.store(r2, rlx)
}
%%
allow (r1 = 42 && r2 = 42) [C11, C17, C20]
forbid (r1 = 42 && r2 = 42) [RC11, IMM, smrd, SC, RA]
